module devcontainer_voice 1.0;

# Host SELinux policy for Claude Code's voice mode in a workbench. See
# docs/LAYERS.md, "Voice", for when it is needed and how to install it.
#
# Voice mode records the microphone through the host's PulseAudio server
# (PipeWire's pipewire-pulse), which runs in the desktop session as
# unconfined_t. `host/workbench voice-setup` gives that server a second
# socket, in a folder labelled container_file_t for the workbench category
# and mounted only into a Claude workbench started with voice on. The file
# checks already allow the workbench to open that socket; what the stock
# policy refuses is the connection itself (EACCES on connect(), measured
# 2026-09-28, through a relay socket in the labelled folder too).
#
# This allows exactly that: container_engine_t, which only the workbench and
# its helpers run in, may connect to a unix stream socket held by an
# unconfined_t process. It still has to reach the socket's file, and every
# host socket outside a folder labelled for it stays out of reach.
# container_t, which ordinary containers run in, is unaffected.

require {
  type container_engine_t;
  type unconfined_t;
  class unix_stream_socket connectto;
}

allow container_engine_t unconfined_t:unix_stream_socket connectto;
